---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Pricing
eyebrow: Services
subtitle: Self-host Project Broadsheet for free, or bring me in to handle setup, migration, hosting, or ongoing care.
permalink: /pricing/
---
<div class="lead" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
  Project Broadsheet is free to fork and free to keep. The pricing below is for the cases where you'd rather not spend a weekend on setup, or where you need help that isn't in the documentation. I take on a small number of engagements at a time.
</div>

<section class="pricing-section">
  <header class="pricing-section__header">
    <h2 class="pricing-section__title">Self-hosted</h2>
    <p class="pricing-section__summary">Fork the repository and deploy it yourself. Every feature ships by default. There is no "pro tier" holding anything back.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="pricing-free">
    <div>
      <span class="pricing-free__price">{{ pricing.selfHosted.price }}<span class="pricing-free__cadence">{{ pricing.selfHosted.cadence }}</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pricing-free__body">
      <h3>{{ pricing.selfHosted.name }}</h3>
      <p>{{ pricing.selfHosted.tagline }}</p>
      <ul class="pricing-card__list">
        {% for f in pricing.selfHosted.features %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="{{ pricing.selfHosted.cta.url }}">{{ pricing.selfHosted.cta.label }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pricing-section" id="launch-packages">
  <header class="pricing-section__header">
    <h2 class="pricing-section__title">Launch packages</h2>
    <p class="pricing-section__summary">Done-with-you setup, branding, and deployment. The package names are shorthand for scope. Pick the one that matches how much help you want.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="pricing-grid">
    {% for pkg in pricing.packages %}
    <article class="pricing-card{% if pkg.featured %} pricing-card--featured{% endif %}">
      {% if pkg.featured %}<span class="pricing-card__tag">Most common</span>{% endif %}
      <h3 class="pricing-card__name">{{ pkg.name }}</h3>
      <div>
        <span class="pricing-card__price">{{ pkg.price }}</span>
        <span class="pricing-card__cadence">{{ pkg.cadence }} · {{ pkg.hours }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="pricing-card__tagline">{{ pkg.tagline }}</p>
      <ul class="pricing-card__list">
        {% for f in pkg.features %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <div class="pricing-card__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--block" href="{{ pkg.cta.url }}">{{ pkg.cta.label }}</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pricing-section" id="migration">
  <header class="pricing-section__header">
    <h2 class="pricing-section__title">Content migration</h2>
    <p class="pricing-section__summary">Moving an archive from Ghost, WordPress, Substack, or Medium. You get clean Markdown, your images preserved, and a redirect map covering every legacy URL.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="migration-grid">
    {% for m in pricing.migration %}
    <div class="tier-row">
      <div class="tier-row__name">{{ m.name }}</div>
      <div class="tier-row__price">{{ m.price }}</div>
      <div class="tier-row__scope">{{ m.scope }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top: var(--space-md); color: var(--text-muted);">Larger archive or unusual source? <a href="/forms/quote-migration/">Request a migration quote</a> and I'll reply personally.</p>
</section>

<section class="pricing-section" id="hosting">
  <header class="pricing-section__header">
    <h2 class="pricing-section__title">Monthly hosting</h2>
    <p class="pricing-section__summary">Managed hosting on my Cloudflare account. You write, I keep the lights on.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="pricing-grid">
    {% for plan in pricing.hosting %}
    <article class="pricing-card{% if plan.featured %} pricing-card--featured{% endif %}">
      {% if plan.featured %}<span class="pricing-card__tag">Most common</span>{% endif %}
      <h3 class="pricing-card__name">{{ plan.name }}</h3>
      <div>
        <span class="pricing-card__price">{{ plan.price }}</span>
        <span class="pricing-card__cadence">{{ plan.cadence }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="pricing-card__tagline">{{ plan.tagline }}</p>
      <ul class="pricing-card__list">
        {% for f in plan.features %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <div class="pricing-card__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--block" href="/forms/hosting-inquiry/?plan={{ plan.slug }}">Inquire</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pricing-section" id="care">
  <header class="pricing-section__header">
    <h2 class="pricing-section__title">Care plans</h2>
    <p class="pricing-section__summary">Ongoing maintenance, content publishing, and priority support for publications that ship regularly. Cancel any month.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="pricing-grid">
    {% for plan in pricing.care %}
    <article class="pricing-card{% if plan.featured %} pricing-card--featured{% endif %}">
      {% if plan.featured %}<span class="pricing-card__tag">Most common</span>{% endif %}
      <h3 class="pricing-card__name">{{ plan.name }}</h3>
      <div>
        <span class="pricing-card__price">{{ plan.price }}</span>
        <span class="pricing-card__cadence">{{ plan.cadence }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="pricing-card__tagline">{{ plan.tagline }}</p>
      <ul class="pricing-card__list">
        {% for f in plan.features %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <div class="pricing-card__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--block" href="/forms/care-inquiry/?plan={{ plan.slug }}">Inquire</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pricing-section" id="hourly">
  <header class="pricing-section__header">
    <h2 class="pricing-section__title">Hourly and training</h2>
    <p class="pricing-section__summary">For custom work, one-off requests, or knowledge transfer.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="hourly-grid">
    {% for h in pricing.hourly %}
    <div class="tier-row">
      <div class="tier-row__name">{{ h.name }}</div>
      <div class="tier-row__price">{{ h.price }} <span class="tier-row__scope">{{ h.cadence }}</span></div>
      <div class="tier-row__desc">{{ h.description }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">
  <div class="callout__title">One person on the other end</div>
  <p>Every engagement is with me. No bots, no AI, no sales team. If you write, I reply. If you book a call, I'm on it. That means occasional delays (I sleep, I have a kid, I write for my own publication too), but it means you always know who you're dealing with.</p>
</div>
